          "candidate_line_count": 2,
          "center_error": 3.894,
          "text": "Measures for the Administration of Domestic Project Operations of CCECC FUZHOU SURVEY & DESIGN INSTITUTE CO."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "chapter_heading",
          "source_block": 3,
          "candidate_block": 3,
          "candidate_line_count": 1,
          "center_error": 3.959,
          "text": "Chapter 1 General Provisions"
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 4,
          "candidate_block": 4,
          "candidate_line_count": 6,
          "center_error": 14.518,
          "text": "Article 1 In accordance with the guiding opinions on high­quality business operations of\nthe joint­stock company, and in combination with the relevant requirements of the\nGroup Company's Implementation Rules for High­Quality Business Operations (Trial)\n(CCECC Operations [2024] No. 341), these Measures are specially formulated to\ncomprehensively improve project operation quality, effectively manage the company's\ndomestic business operations, and standardize business procedures and workflows."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 8,
          "candidate_block": 5,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 14.914,
          "text": "Article 2 Projects in these Measures refer to various types of the Company's\nbusiness operations undertaken through direct entrustment or bidding, such as\nconsulting, survey, design, supervision, and engineering general contracting."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 10,
          "candidate_block": 6,
          "candidate_line_count": 4,
          "center_error": 15.291,
          "text": "Article 3 In principle, business undertaking work shall follow the procedure of project evaluation first, then\napplication for approval, and finally contract signing. Article 4 When carrying out project business undertaking\nwork, factors such as the Company's development strategy, business direction, responsibility cost, production\nand technical capabilities, and current status"
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 12,
          "candidate_block": 7,
          "candidate_line_count": 5,
          "center_error": 12.733,
          "text": "Article 4 shall be comprehensively considered. In accordance with the\nprocedural provisions of these Measures, the work of links such as \"information\ntracking, project evaluation and application, bid document preparation and\nreview, contract negotiation, contract review and signing, owner services during\nproject implementation, and project return visits\" shall be completed."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "chapter_heading",
          "source_block": 17,
          "candidate_block": 8,
          "candidate_line_count": 1,
          "center_error": 3.891,
          "text": "Chapter 2 Relevant Responsibilities"
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 18,
          "candidate_block": 9,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 16.098,
          "text": "Article 5 The Business Development Department is the management department\nfor the Company's domestic project business work and is responsible for the\nlayout and development of the institute's business market."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 20,
          "candidate_block": 10,
          "candidate_line_count": 2,
          "center_error": 22.561,
          "text": "Article 6 The relevant personnel and main responsibilities involved in project\nbusiness operations are shown in Table 1 as follows:"
